  "id": "word-blindness",
  "term": "word blindness",
  "definition": "Word blindness is a cognitive disorder in which a person has difficulty understanding written or printed words even though vision is intact. It can be present from development or acquired later, and in developmental forms it can interfere substantially with reading performance and daily activities that depend on reading.",
